# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for CRRT-dose-lmtp
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A RULE.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC, because it ships to consortium sites. That decides what
# belongs in git:
#
#   .claude/   IGNORED, and a symlink to ../crrt-manuscript-tools/lmtp-claude.
#              It holds the LMTP feasibility audit, which names ten sites with
#              their dose distributions, coverage and positivity-exclusion status,
#              plus internal deliberations. None of that can be public. The
#              private repo is the backed-up copy of record; this is only a view
#              of it so Claude Code can read it locally.
#   CLAUDE.md  TRACKED. Deliberately written with no site named: it says "the
#              coordinating site" and "one participating institution" throughout.
#              It is useful to anyone working on this code, so it ships.
#   docs/      IGNORED, and a symlink to ../crrt-manuscript-tools/lmtp-docs.
#              The cohort tutorial is built around worked numbers from the
#              coordinating site: its cohort counts, its mortality rate, and a
#              detailed account of its EHR charting defects.
#              Naming only UCMC was the wrong test; the content is the issue.
#              A site-facing METHODS.md without site-specific numbers should
#              replace it here.
#
# Before adding a tracked file, ask whether it carries any site's numbers, not
# just whether it names a site.
# History was rewritten on 2026-08-18 to purge .claude/ and docs/ from history, so
# do not restore either by un-ignoring it.
# =============================================================================

# --- Site configuration (never leaves the site) ------------------------------
config/config.json
config/config_*.json
!config/config_template.json

# --- Data: raw CLIF tables must never be committed ---------------------------
CLIF_*.parquet
CLIF_*.csv
CLIF_*.fst
*.RData

# --- Outputs -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore output contents, keep the READMEs that explain the layout.
output/**
!output/README.md
!output/final_no_phi/
!output/final_no_phi/README.md
!output/intermediate_phi/
!output/intermediate_phi/README.md

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R / renv ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit renv.lock, renv/activate.R and renv/settings.json; ignore only the
# local library. .Rprofile is intentionally NOT ignored: it sources
# renv/activate.R and must ship so every site uses the pinned library.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
renv/sandbox/
.Rhistory
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# --- Internal planning and docs: symlinked to the private repo, never tracked --
.claude
.claude/
docs
docs/

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
# .vscode is tracked only for the two files that make the repo work correctly
# out of the box (interpreter path, recommended extensions). Personal settings
# like launch.json stay local.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Rendered artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: deliberately NOT a blanket `*.pdf` / `*.html` ignore (the sibling repo
# has one). Figures and rendered reports are the product here, so only the
# transient R plot dump is excluded.
Rplots.pdf
